Today when `subobjects` are disabled (auto flattening) and a mapping contains multiple `dynamic` configurations then validation kicks to avoid creating the mapping. This can happen if for example at the root level `dynamic` is set to `false`, but an object field mapper sets `dynamic` to `true`. This is because an object mapping is flattened and mappings today don't make a decision which `dynamic` attribute wins. This now happens by default if index mode is strictly columnar.

In a flattened mapping, the dynamic behaviour should be expressed at a prefix. For example: `dynamic.false: *` and `dynamic.true: attributes.resources.*`, this way mappings don't have to make a decision. Also we might be able to extract these field patterns from how dynamic is currently configured in mappings.

